<article class="env-definition" id="084L">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/084L">Definition <span data-tag="084L">28.25.6</span>.</a> Let $X$ be a scheme. Let $T \subset X$ be a closed subset whose complement is retrocompact in $X$. Let $\mathcal{F}$ be a quasi-coherent $\mathcal{O}_ X$-module. The quasi-coherent subsheaf $\mathcal{F}' \subset \mathcal{F}$ defined in Lemma <a href="/tag/07ZP" data-tag="07ZP">28.25.5</a> is called the <em>subsheaf of sections supported on $T$</em>. </p>
</article>